        'Yes, mild swelling in your feet, ankles, and lower legs is a normal part of pregnancy, especially from the second trimester onward, caused by fluid retention and your growing womb affecting circulation. What\'s different with preeclampsia is swelling that\'s sudden, severe, or affects your hands and face, especially alongside other symptoms like headache or vision changes.',
